Suppose we have a relation $\mathrm{R}(\mathrm{A}, \mathrm{B}, \mathrm{C}, \mathrm{D}, \mathrm{E}, \mathrm{F})$ with functional dependencies(FDs):
$$
\begin{aligned}
& \mathrm{A} \rightarrow \mathrm{B} \\
& \mathrm{BCD} \rightarrow \mathrm{E} \\
& \mathrm{E} \rightarrow \mathrm{F}
\end{aligned}
$$
Suppose there are at most $2$ different values for each of attributes $\text{A, C},$ and $\text{D}$. What is the maximum number of different values for attribute $\text{F}?$
